# {Topic} — Formal Hypothesis Specification

## 1. Formal Hypotheses
* **Null Hypothesis ($H_0$):** Application of {Technique X} yields no statistically significant improvement in {Metric Y} compared to baseline ($p \ge 0.05$).
* **Alternative Hypothesis ($H_1$):** Application of {Technique X} achieves $\ge 20\%$ reduction in {Metric Y} with $p < 0.01$ under identical workloads.

## 2. Variable Operationalization
| Variable Name | Variable Type | Operational Definition | Measurement Unit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Parameter Weight Quantization | Independent | Quantization precision (FP16, INT8, INT4) | Bit-width |
| Inference Latency | Dependent | Time to First Token (TTFT) | Milliseconds ($p99\text{ ms}$) |
| Batch Size | Controlled | Concurrency load held static at $B=32$ | Concurrent Streams |

## 3. Statistical Power & Validation Criteria
* **Alpha Level ($\alpha$):** $0.01$
* **Statistical Test:** Two-tailed Welch's $t$-test / Mann-Whitney $U$ test.
* **Sample Size:** $N \ge 1,000$ independent trials per condition.
